# Photo Import — example camera profiles
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# You normally never edit this by hand: run `photo-import` and the first-run
# wizard builds ~/.config/photo-import/cameras.conf for you, and
# `photo-import --config-update` edits it later. This file just shows the
# format if you'd rather write it yourself.
#
# One profile per line, fields separated by "|":
#
#   Name | raw_exts | jpeg_exts | split_folders | output_base_dir
#
#   raw_exts / jpeg_exts   comma-separated extensions, matched case-insensitively.
#                          Either (or both) may be blank:
#                            both set    -> files route by extension
#                            one blank   -> single-file-type source (a TIFF scanner)
#                            both blank  -> catch-all, every file is copied
#   split_folders          true  -> <album>/raws/ and <album>/jpgs/
#                          false -> everything at the album root
#   output_base_dir        absolute path (no ~); albums are created inside it
#
# Camera auto-detection looks for each profile's raw_exts on the card. Put more
# specific profiles first.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

Sony A7 IV|ARW|JPG,JPEG|true|/Users/you/Pictures/Sony A7 IV
Fujifilm X-T5|RAF|JPG,JPEG|true|/Users/you/Pictures/Fujifilm X-T5
Film Scans|TIF,TIFF||false|/Users/you/Pictures/Film Scans
